# Keys of the device tree list in the initramfs (boot-dtb-select D7), read by lume-bootsel
# from /etc/bootsel-keys. <role>=<key>[,<key>...], with names of linux/input-event-codes.h
# or numbers. select: held at power on, opens the list. pageup/pagedown (optional) jump a
# screen in the long list of converted device trees.
#
# PROVISIONAL until proof 1.2 tells which keys the factory U-Boot of the R36S already reads
# at power on (pins C0, C2 and C5).
# All in gpio-keys (built in). A is BTN_EAST in the R36S device tree (the right button).
select=KEY_VOLUMEDOWN
up=BTN_DPAD_UP,KEY_VOLUMEUP
down=BTN_DPAD_DOWN,KEY_VOLUMEDOWN
ok=BTN_EAST
pageup=BTN_DPAD_LEFT,BTN_TL
pagedown=BTN_DPAD_RIGHT,BTN_TR
